    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a clear primary engine in **Corbin Carroll**, whose 87.13 score is the unequivocal ceiling play of the day. With a prime spot in the two-hole against Feltner (4.96 xERA), **Corbin Carroll** is perfectly positioned to leverage his elite speed, our most critical scarcity anchor. Complementing him is **Mickey Moniak**, who boasts a robust 75.75 score; his favorable platoon advantage against the right-handed Kelly and a soft matchup profile make him an essential start. **Gabriel Moreno** and **Isaac Paredes** also grade out as elite options today, both benefiting significantly from their high-order placement and projected success against vulnerable starters in Feltner and Houser, respectively.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the card was the final UTIL spot, where **Austin Riley** (58.74) barely edged out **Tyler Soderstrom** (57.87) for the primary lineup, though both are currently active. **Tyler Soderstrom** carries higher risk due to a tough matchup against Rasmussen (3.17 xERA), which suppresses his scoring despite his strong batting order placement. Meanwhile, **Max Muncy** and **Henry Bolte** are skating on thin ice today with scores of 42.29 and 41.35; while they remain in the lineup due to our current depth constraints, they are hovering just above the \"Below floor\" threshold. We remain cognizant that **James Wood**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, and **Giancarlo Stanton** remain sidelined, while **Jose Caballero** failed to crack the starting rotation today, leaving us thin on bench utility. Owners should monitor the Rasmussen start closely; should the game environment shift or a late-inning defensive replacement occur, we risk eroding our narrow batting average margins, particularly with **Max Muncy** struggling against elite-tier pitching.",
